## What was wrong

Both bugs were in `src/retry.js`:

1. **`Retry-After: 0` was discarded.** `parseRetryAfter` only accepted delta-seconds when `seconds > 0`, so `"0"` fell through to the missing-header path and returned the 1000 ms default. Now any non-negative integer is accepted verbatim, so `0` means "retry immediately."

2. **Date-form values ignored `receivedAt`.** `waitFor` measured `parsed.ms - now`, where `now` defaults to `Date.now()` — the wall clock at evaluation time, not the moment the response arrived. `response.receivedAt` was part of the documented response shape but never read, so a slow response pushed the deadline out and made the client wait the full interval all over again. Now the reference is `response?.receivedAt ?? now`, clamped at 0.

